  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/micro-elements/MicroElements.Swashbuckle.FluentValidation",
  "published": "2026-11-27T07:25:10.19Z",
  "releaseNotes": "$# Changes in 7.3.3\n\n- Fixed OpenAPI generation for `NotEmpty()` on GUIDs and date/time values with a recognized string format. These properties stay required without acquiring `minLength: 1`. CLR strings retain their minimum length, including strings explicitly mapped to `uuid`. [#244](https://github.com/micro-elements/MicroElements.Swashbuckle.FluentValidation/issues/244)\n\n# Changes in 7.3.2\n\n- Fix multipart request-body rules on .NET 10 with Swashbuckle 11.0.1. The same adapter assembly also supports Swashbuckle 10.2.1. [#241](https://github.com/micro-elements/MicroElements.Swashbuckle.FluentValidation/issues/241)\n\n# Changes in 7.3.1\n- Fixed array length constraints for MVC query parameters in `MicroElements.AspNetCore.OpenApi.FluentValidation`. Collection length validators now emit `minItems` and `maxItems`, preserve the item schema, and respect stricter bounds already in the OpenAPI document.\n- Element length rules configured with `RuleForEach` no longer produce a collection count limit. [Issue #239](https://github.com/micro-elements/MicroElements.Swashbuckle.FluentValidation/issues/239)\n\n# Changes in 7.3.0\n- Added: stable `net11.0` assets for the shared core, native ASP.NET Core OpenAPI adapter, and Swashbuckle adapter. The net11 Swashbuckle asset uses stable Swashbuckle 11.0.1 / Microsoft.OpenApi 3.11.0 and supports explicitly selected OpenAPI 3.2. Existing net8/net9/net10 Swashbuckle dependency families are preserved.\n- Added: native OpenAPI 3.2 and explicitly selected 3.1 coverage at runtime and build time, preserving FluentValidation constraints on properties, child validators, collection items, parameters, forms, and shared schemas. .NET 11 dependencies and SDK baseline now use GA versions.\n- Security: the native net10 adapter requires Microsoft.OpenApi 2.7.5 or later, excluding versions affected by GHSA-v5pm-xwqc-g5wc.\n- Behavior: .NET 11 float/double bounds preserve the runtime's decimal conversion values without extra library rounding. Existing .NET 8–10 behavior and NSwag package targets are retained; existing NSwag assets are tested on a .NET 11 host.\n- Includes the 7.2.4 fix for untyped string length constraints (#238). Source builds require SDK 11.0.100 or an eligible newer 11.0 feature band. MyGet publication is manual and restricted to the release tag.\n\n# Changes in 7.3.0-beta.1\n- Security: the native ASP.NET Core OpenAPI adapter now requires `Microsoft.OpenApi` 2.7.5 or later on net10, excluding versions affected by GHSA-v5pm-xwqc-g5wc.\n- Added: `net11.0` assets for `MicroElements.OpenApi.FluentValidation` and `MicroElements.AspNetCore.OpenApi.FluentValidation`, using .NET 11 RC3 dependencies. The native ASP.NET Core adapter supports OpenAPI 3.2 and explicitly selected OpenAPI 3.1, with runtime and build-time generation coverage.\n- Compatibility: Swashbuckle and NSwag retain their existing package targets and generator dependencies. Their existing assets were tested in .NET 11 hosts. This beta does not include the separate Swashbuckle 11 / Microsoft.OpenApi 3.x experiment.\n- Behavior: on .NET 11, float and double validation bounds can appear with additional decimal digits in generated schemas because of runtime numeric conversion changes. The library preserves the runtime values without additional rounding; existing .NET 8–10 behavior is unchanged.\n- Development: added a shared .NET 11 RC3 SDK baseline with `rollForward: latestFeature`. Package consumers do not need this SDK unless targeting .NET 11. Automatic package upload remains disabled; beta publication requires a manually triggered workflow on the beta tag.\n\n\nFull release notes can be found at: https://github.com/micro-elements/MicroElements.Swashbuckle.FluentValidation/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
